# What never belongs in the build context.
#
# The build stage runs Gradle inside the image, so the context is the source tree and nothing
# that a previous build, a running node or an IDE left beside it. Keeping those out is not only
# about upload size: build/ holds jars compiled against another JDK, data/ holds a live engine's
# segments and write-ahead logs, and /excalibur.properties is the gitignored working copy that
# may carry a real EXCALIBUR_LLM_API_KEY.
#
# The build stage compiles and packages; it runs no tests (-x test in the Dockerfile), so the
# context has to hold what the compiler and the packaging tasks read and nothing more. The files
# only tests read - the README and the properties template that ConfigKeyInventoryTest checks,
# the git history RepositoryCompletenessTest asks - are free to stay out.
#
# Every pattern here is matched against the path from the context root, not against a file name
# anywhere in the tree: "*.log" excludes a log at the root and nowhere else. A rule meant for
# every directory says so with "**/". The directory rules below are written for the root and for
# one module level instead, because a "**/build/" would also match the Java packages named build
# that this repository has, and would remove their sources from the context.

# Build outputs, at the root and in each module.
/build/
*/build/
*/out/
*/target/
**/*.class
**/*.war

# Gradle state. The wrapper jar and its properties are required by the build stage and must
# survive the exclusion above them.
.gradle/
*/.gradle/
gradle/wrapper/dists/
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties

# Version control and CI metadata.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Engine runtime state: segments, write-ahead logs, catalogs, per-segment index files - whether
# a node ran from the root or from inside a module.
/data/
*/data/
**/*.db
**/*.dat
**/*.wal
**/*.idx
**/*.csr
**/*.hnsw
**/*.lsh
**/*.hprof

# Local configuration. The working copy may hold a real API key. Anchored, so the packaged
# default at excalibur-api/src/main/resources/excalibur.properties - which the node falls back
# to from the classpath - is still copied in.
/excalibur.properties

# IDE and editor state.
.idea/
*/.idea/
.vscode/
**/*.iml
**/*.ipr
**/*.iws
**/.classpath
**/.project
**/.factorypath
**/.settings/
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*~

# Logs, benchmark output and scratch.
**/*.log
**/jmh-results/
**/benchmark-results/
/tmp/
/temp/
**/*.tmp

# Documentation, the properties template, and the image's own inputs: nothing the build stage
# runs reads any of them.
**/*.md
excalibur.properties.example
LICENSE
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
